# Margince skill

This folder lets an AI tool work in Margince as you. The tool calls the Margince API at
`{{.BaseURL}}` with your agent passport, and can do what you can do there with the
permissions you ticked on that passport, and nothing more.

The folder holds four files:

- `SKILL.md`: the rules the AI tool follows.
- `INDEX.md`: every call a passport can make, one row each.
- `openapi.yaml`: those calls in full.
- `README.md`: this page.

No passport is in this folder. You save it apart, so one download serves every
passport you make.

## Save your passport

Create a passport in Margince under **Settings → Agents**, and copy it. It is shown once.
Never type it on a command line, where your shell history keeps it. Save it in one
of these places, under the name `MARGINCE_PASSPORT`:

- **macOS Keychain.** Run the command below. It asks for the passport and keeps it in
  your login keychain.

  ```sh
  security add-generic-password -a "$USER" -s MARGINCE_PASSPORT -w
  ```

- **1Password.** Save it as an item, and give the AI tool the item's reference, for
  example `op://Private/Margince passport/credential`.
- **Your shell, for this session only.** Run the command below and paste the passport
  when it waits. Nothing is shown and nothing is written to your history.

  ```sh
  read -rs MARGINCE_PASSPORT && export MARGINCE_PASSPORT
  ```

The AI tool reads the passport from `MARGINCE_PASSPORT` only, so set it in the shell
you start the tool from. From the Keychain:

```sh
export MARGINCE_PASSPORT="$(security find-generic-password -s MARGINCE_PASSPORT -w)"
```

From 1Password: `export MARGINCE_PASSPORT="$(op read '<item reference>')"`.

## Install the skill

Unzip `margince-skill.zip`. It holds one folder, `margince`.

- **Claude Code.** Move the `margince` folder to `~/.claude/skills/margince`. Claude finds
  it the next time it starts.
- **Claude Desktop.** Add `margince-skill.zip` as a skill in the app's settings.
- **Codex.** Move the folder where you keep such files, for example `~/margince`, and
  add this line to your `AGENTS.md`: "To work in Margince, read `~/margince/SKILL.md`
  first."
- **Gemini CLI and Antigravity.** Move the folder the same way, and add the same line to
  your `GEMINI.md`.

## Try it

With the passport in `MARGINCE_PASSPORT`, this lists one company you can see:

```sh
curl '{{.BaseURL}}/companies?limit=1' -H "Authorization: Bearer $MARGINCE_PASSPORT"
```

## When a passport ends

A passport made in Settings lasts 30 days. To stop an agent sooner, choose **Revoke** on
the passport in **Settings → Agents**. It loses access on its next call. Then make a new
passport and save it under the same name. The skill does not change.
